---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { useStoryblokApi } from "@storyblok/astro";
import HeroText from "../components/HeroText.astro";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { getStoryblokVersion } from "../utils/storyblok";
import img2016 from "../assets/images/timeline/2016_esme_fairbairn_logo.jpg";
import img2017 from "../assets/images/timeline/2017_seaside_conference.jpg";
import img2022 from "../assets/images/timeline/2022_first_online_seminar_image.jpg";
import img2023a from "../assets/images/timeline/2023_bucket_and_spade_winners_blackpool.jpg";
import img2023b from "../assets/images/timeline/2023_walking_tour_weston.jpg";
import img2025a from "../assets/images/timeline/2025_national_seaside_day.png";
import img2025b from "../assets/images/timeline/2025_recognising_seaside_heritage_conference.jpg";
import img2026a from "../assets/images/timeline/2026_walking_tour_sussex_coast.jpg";
import img2026b from "../assets/images/timeline/2026_valuing_seaside_heritage_conference_saltdean.jpg";

const storyblokApi = useStoryblokApi();
const { data: homeData } = await storyblokApi.get("cdn/stories/home", {
  version: getStoryblokVersion(Astro.request),
});
const signupLink =
  homeData?.story?.content?.signup_link?.url ??
  "https://piers.us9.list-manage.com/subscribe?u=bc30e2a33dfae5ee4abdf15e8&id=7ab71caf2f";

const metadata = {
  siteTitle: "Seaside Heritage Network",
  pageTitle: "About the Network",
};

const linkClass = "underline decoration-1 hover:decoration-2";
const imgClass = "w-full rounded object-cover aspect-[16/9]";
---

<PageLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <HeroText tagline="About" title="About the Network" />
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-8 pb-12 sm:pb-16 sm:px-6">
    <ol class="relative border-l-4 border-accent pl-8" role="list">
      <li class="relative mb-10">
        <span
          class="absolute -left-11 top-0 h-5 w-5 rounded-full bg-accent"
          aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold leading-tight">2016</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-4 items-start">
          <p class="flex-1">
            The Seaside Heritage Network was first formed in 2016 by <a
              href="https://scarboroughmuseumsandgalleries.org.uk/"
              class={linkClass}>Scarborough Museum Trust</a
            > with funding support from the Esme Fairbairn Foundation. Its founding
            members included Southend Museums Service, Hastings Museum and Art Gallery,
            Manx National Heritage, Blackpool Museum Project and the National Piers
            Society.
          </p>
          <Image
            src={img2016}
            alt="Esmée Fairbairn Foundation logo"
            class="rounded border border-white/10 bg-white px-1 w-full lg:w-[280px] lg:shrink-0"
            widths={[280, 560, 800]}
            sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 280px"
          />
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The original SHN had a museum focus, with an emphasis on utilising the
          network to research seaside-related collections, locate custodians of
          seaside heritage and share vital knowledge and expertise. However, the
          activities of the early SHN were unable to continue once the funding
          ended.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="relative mb-10">
        <span
          class="absolute -left-11 top-1 h-5 w-5 rounded-full bg-accent"
          aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold leading-tight">2017</h2>
          <span class="text-sm text-gray-400">April</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          The SHN held the 'Seaside Heritage Conference' at Scarborough Spa,
          with speakers including current SHN trustees Samantha Richardson,
          Kathryn Ferry, and Anya Chapman.
        </p>
        <figure class="mt-4">
          <Image
            src={img2017}
            alt="Beside the Seaside conference brochure, Scarborough Spa, April 2017"
            class={imgClass}
            widths={[600, 1200]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 672px"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">
            Seaside Heritage Conference at Scarborough Spa
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </li>

      <li class="relative mb-10">
        <span
          class="absolute -left-11 top-1 h-5 w-5 rounded-full bg-accent"
          aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold leading-tight">2022</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          A small group of volunteers with interests in the heritage of seaside
          tourism sought to re-establish the Seaside Heritage Network, with a
          broader focus. With the full support of Scarborough Museums and
          Galleries, they took over the original name and logo.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The 'new' SHN began by providing free online seminars that examined
          particular examples and issues relating to seaside heritage. These <a
            href="https://www.youtube.com/@SeasideHeritageNetwork"
            class={linkClass}>seminars can be viewed on our YouTube channel</a
          >. Attendance steadily increased, recognising a clear community of
          people who valued the distinctive heritage of the seaside.
        </p>
        <figure class="mt-4">
          <Image
            src={img2022}
            alt="Seaside Heritage Network online seminar: Big Heritage — Issues, Challenges, Opportunities"
            class={imgClass}
            widths={[600, 1200]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 672px"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">
            First online seminar
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </li>

      <li class="relative mb-10">
        <span
          class="absolute -left-11 top-1 h-5 w-5 rounded-full bg-accent"
          aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold leading-tight">2023</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          The annual 'Bucket and Spade' list was introduced, inviting members of
          the public to vote on their favourite example of seaside heritage. The
          inaugural winner was Saltburn Cliff Railway. The SHN also introduced
          #NationalSeasideDay on 1 July.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The annual 'Big Day Out' — an in-person event held in a seaside town
          to celebrate seaside heritage and announce the winner of the Bucket
          and Spade list — was also launched. Previous locations have included
          Blackpool, Weston-Super-Mare, and Scarborough. The event includes an
          informal interview with somebody who has championed the UK seaside
          (previous guests have included the designer Wayne Hemingway and the
          author Paul Doe).
        </p>
        <figure class="mt-4">
          <Image
            src={img2023a}
            alt="Bucket and Spade list winners at the Big Day Out, Blackpool 2023"
            class={imgClass}
            widths={[600, 1200]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 672px"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">
            Bucket and Spade winners in Blackpool
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The SHN has also been increasingly active in organising guided tours
          of seaside resorts, with recent examples including Blackpool,
          Weymouth, Weston-Super-Mare, Brighton, Saltdean, and Margate.
        </p>
        <figure class="mt-4">
          <Image
            src={img2023b}
            alt="Guided walking tour of Weston-super-Mare, 2023"
            class={imgClass}
            widths={[600, 1200]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 672px"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">
            Walking tour of Weston-Super-Mare
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </li>

      <li class="relative mb-10">
        <span
          class="absolute -left-11 top-1 h-5 w-5 rounded-full bg-accent"
          aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold leading-tight">2025</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          From 2025, attendees at the online seminars and the wider public were
          invited to nominate their favourite examples of seaside heritage —
          these were whittled down to a shortlist which was then put to a public
          vote.
        </p>
        <figure class="mt-4">
          <Image
            src={img2025a}
            alt="National Seaside Day, 1st July 2025"
            class="rounded w-full max-w-[420px] border border-white/20"
            widths={[420, 840]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 420px"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">
            National Seaside Day
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The Seaside Heritage Network also teamed up with <a
            href="https://hbap.org.uk/"
            class={linkClass}>Historic Buildings and Places</a
          > to organise in-person symposia on seaside heritage. The first symposium,
          'Recognising Seaside Heritage', was held in London in June 2025.
        </p>
        <figure class="mt-4">
          <Image
            src={img2025b}
            alt="Recognising Seaside Heritage symposium, London, June 2025"
            class={imgClass}
            widths={[600, 1200]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 672px"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">
            Recognising Seaside Heritage symposium
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mt-4">
          In December 2025, the Seaside Heritage Network was registered as a
          charity (a 'Foundation CIO') with the Charities Commission — an
          educational charity which seeks to raise awareness and understanding
          of the broad heritage associated with the UK seaside holiday.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="relative mb-10">
        <span
          class="absolute -left-11 top-1 h-5 w-5 rounded-full bg-accent"
          aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold leading-tight">2026</h2>
          <span class="text-sm text-gray-400">June</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          The second symposium, 'Valuing Seaside Heritage', was held at Saltdean
          Lido. A third symposium is planned for 2027.
        </p>
        <figure class="mt-4">
          <Image
            src={img2026b}
            alt="Valuing Seaside Heritage symposium at Saltdean Lido, June 2026"
            class={imgClass}
            widths={[600, 1200]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 672px"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">
            Valuing Seaside Heritage conference Saltdean
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="mt-4">
          <Image
            src={img2026a}
            alt="Guided walking tour of the Sussex coast, 2026"
            class={imgClass}
            widths={[600, 1200]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 672px"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">
            Walking tour of the Sussex coast
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="pl-8 mt-10">
      The Seaside Heritage Network is not a membership organisation, but if you
      are interested in our activities you can <a
        href={signupLink}
        class={linkClass}>sign up to our newsletter</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
